@page "/wiki/authorities"
@page "/wiki/authorities/{Key}"

@*
    The authorities, which say who rules and how they are replaced.

    Eight of them, and almost the whole of what tells them apart is in three facts rather than in
    their prose: whether there are elections, whether there is an heir, and what an authority forces
    onto the founding species. A hive mind's founders are hive-minded whatever else was wanted for
    them, which is a cost worth seeing before it is paid.

    The second address is one entry of the shelf. It shows the same page and picks that one out, so a
    reader who found the thing they came for can send somebody straight to it rather than to a list
    with an instruction to scroll.
*@

<PageTitle>Authorities - Stellaris Empire Manager</PageTitle>

<WikiSection Kind="WikiKind.Authorities" Focus="@Key" />

@code {
    /// <summary>The entry the address names, where it names one.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Key { get; set; }
}
